  "purpose": "<p>The Joint Committee on Human Rights consists of twelve members, appointed from both the House of Commons and the House of Lords, to examine matters relating to human rights within the United Kingdom, as well as scrutinising every Government Bill for its compatibility with human rights.</p>\r\n<p>Follow us on social media:&nbsp;<u><a href=\"https://bsky.app/profile/hoccommittees.parliament.uk\">Bluesky</a></u>&nbsp;| <u><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/profile.php?id=61579513151155\">Facebook</a></u>&nbsp;|&nbsp;<u><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/ukcommonscommittees\">Instagram</a></u>&nbsp;| <u><a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/showcase/house-of-commons-committees\">LinkedIn</a></u>&nbsp;| <u><a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/user/UKCommonsCommittees/\">Reddit</a></u>&nbsp;| <u><a href=\"https://x.com/HoCcommitteesUK\">X</a></u>&nbsp;| <u><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLj3mInRJqIekxA--aDW780T_TUCwjea4M\">YouTube</a></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p>View the old&nbsp;<a href=\"https://x.com/HumanRightsCtte\">X account</a>.</p>\r\n<p>Sign up to the weekly <a href=\"https://mailchi.mp/email/committeecorridor\">cross-committee newsletter, ‘Committee Corridor</a>.</p>",
